8. COMMON GITHUB TASKS
============================================================

The following are additional tasks to understand when working with GitHub.

8.1 Clone Using the VS Code UI

VS Code provides a graphical interface for cloning repositories.

You can use the Source Control interface or the Command Palette to access repository cloning options.

8.2 Understanding Private vs Public Repositories

Public Repository:
- Anyone can view the repository.
- Useful for open-source projects.
- Suitable for sharing your portfolio.

Private Repository:
- Access is restricted to you and authorized collaborators.
- Useful for personal projects and private development.
- Suitable for projects that should not be publicly accessible.

8.3 Understanding the .gitignore File

The ".gitignore" file prevents specified files and directories from being tracked by Git.

Common Python exclusions:

    .venv/
    .env
    __pycache__/
    *.pyc
    .DS_Store

Always configure ".gitignore" before your first commit.

